IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa6-offence-of-failure-to-notify.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 12 (Company secretaries): s 279M, "Secretary
-- or joint secretary: offence of failure to notify of changes" (lines 3706-3713 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1 of the part agent coa6.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa6-private-and-public.l4. JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE the text's no in its own words
-- (an "if" that fails); NOTHING "not covered" (an offence limited by its own wording such as "without reasonable excuse" or "who is
-- in default", a person the text does not name, a conviction the text does not describe). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- SEAMS (inputs, named for the section that answers; this module imports coa-core only):
--   ss 279G, 279H, 279I  whether the company has failed to comply (coa6-notification-of-changes.l4: `... has failed to comply with
--                        section 279G` and its two sisters, MAYBE BOOLEAN);
--   s 1121  whether the officer is in default (coa24);   s 251  whether the person is a shadow director (coa5);
--   s 1173(1)  whether the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate (the keel).

§ `Part 12 -- Company secretaries`

§§ `Secretary or joint secretary: offence of failure to notify of changes`

-- ---- s 279M(1): the failure -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "fails ... to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I": any of the three failed. JUST TRUE if any failed; JUST FALSE only if none
-- did; NOTHING while a section's period is still running or an answer is not settled.
-- src:3707 | (1) If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I, an offence is committed by—
@ref s 279M(1) Failure to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I (src:3707)
GIVEN `s 279G the company has failed to comply with section 279G` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 279H the company has failed to comply with section 279H` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 279I the company has failed to comply with section 279I` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279M(1) the company has failed to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I` MEANS
    IF       (`s 279G the company has failed to comply with section 279G` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         OR  (`s 279H the company has failed to comply with section 279H` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         OR  (`s 279I the company has failed to comply with section 279I` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF       (`s 279G the company has failed to comply with section 279G` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
              AND (`s 279H the company has failed to comply with section 279H` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
              AND (`s 279I the company has failed to comply with section 279I` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails ... to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I" (none of the three has failed)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a failure is not settled (a period is still running, or the answer of s 279G, 279H or 279I is not settled)

-- (1)(a): the company commits the offence "if" it fails, "without reasonable excuse". A company that failed but had a reasonable
-- excuse falls outside the offence's own wording: NOTHING (fork F-excuse in NOTES.md).
-- src:3707 | (1) If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I, an offence is committed by—
-- src:3708 | (a) the company, and
@ref s 279M(1)(a) Offence: the company (src:3707-3708)
GIVEN `s 279M(1) the company has failed to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company had a reasonable excuse for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279M(1)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 279M(1) the company has failed to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I, an offence is committed by (a) the company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a company fails ... to comply" (whether it has failed is not yet settled)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the company had a reasonable excuse for the failure`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without reasonable excuse"
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2): "For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company."
-- src:3710 | (2) For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 279M(2) A shadow director is treated as an officer (src:3710)
GIVEN `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279M(2) a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 251 the person is a shadow director`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a shadow director is treated as an officer" says nothing of a person who is not one
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 251 does not say whether the person is a shadow director

-- (1)(b): "every officer of the company who is in default". The person is an officer if the keel's s 1173(1) says so (it answers
-- NOTHING for "another position": "includes") or is a shadow director (s 279M(2)).
-- src:3707 | (1) If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I, an offence is committed by—
-- src:3709 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:3710 | (2) For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 279M(1)(b) Offence: every officer in default (src:3707-3710)
GIVEN `s 279M(1) the company has failed to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company had a reasonable excuse for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279M(1)(b) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 279M(1) the company has failed to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I, an offence is committed by ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a company fails ... to comply" (whether it has failed is not yet settled)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the company had a reasonable excuse for the failure`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without reasonable excuse"
        ELSE IF       (`s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
                  OR  (`s 279M(2) a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company` `s 251 the person is a shadow director` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
             THEN CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
                  WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                  WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 does not say whether the officer is in default
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by (a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default" names no one else

-- ---- s 279M(3): the penalty --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "liable on summary conviction (a) in England and Wales, to a fine; (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding
-- level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the
-- standard scale." In the core's Penalty, a NOTHING field means the text states none: for England and Wales "a fine" states no limit
-- and no daily default fine, and there is no imprisonment anywhere in the section.
-- src:3711 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:3712 | (a) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:3713 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 279M(3) Penalty (src:3711-3713)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 279M(3) the penalty on a person guilty of an offence under section 279M` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
                       , NOTHING
                       , JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
                       , NOTHING
                       , FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`
                       , NOTHING
                       , JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
                       , JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
                       , FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
                       , NOTHING
                       , JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
                       , JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
                       , FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives one penalty for England and Wales and another for Scotland or Northern Ireland, and a conviction in no stated place is neither
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "liable on summary conviction"

-- In pounds. The pounds that level 5 stands for are not in the Act: an input.
-- src:3713 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 279M(3)(b) Penalty: the fine in pounds (src:3713)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 279M(3) the most the person may be fined, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "to a fine" states no amount and no limit
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty depends on the place of conviction, which is not stated
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "liable on summary conviction"

-- src:3713 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 279M(3)(b) Penalty: the daily default fine in pounds (src:3713)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 279M(3) the most the daily default fine may be, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (`the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` DIVIDED BY 10)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (`the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` DIVIDED BY 10)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "(a) in England and Wales, to a fine" states no daily default fine
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty depends on the place of conviction, which is not stated
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "liable on summary conviction"
